From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:48:40 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: core: Don't pin CPU latency on hosts whose clocks
 stay on

ufshcd_setup_clocks() sets the host's CPU latency request to 0 whenever
it turns the clocks on, on hosts without clock scaling, and back to the
default when they turn off. On a host that has neither clock scaling,
clock gating nor runtime autosuspend, the clocks are turned on once at
probe and stay on until system suspend, so the request holds every CPU
in its shallowest idle state for as long as the system runs.

That is the Tensor G4 (zumapro) host today: on a Pixel 9a,
/dev/cpu_dma_latency read 0 and the CPUs' psci sleep states got 0 % of
idle time. With the request off (pm_qos_enable = 0) they got 75 %, over
45 s of idle with the desktop up. Storage stayed clean: 4.5 GB read and
300 MB written at 302 MB/s with no UFS errors. A cold read of /usr/lib
(many small files) took 2-17 % longer without the request, which is the
cost of waking from the deeper state on completion.

Only add the request on hosts that can turn their clocks off. Others
start without it, and pm_qos_enable can still turn it on.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
index dfbcf036d..03967003a 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/core/ufshcd.c
@@ -11403,7 +11403,16 @@ int ufshcd_init(struct ufs_hba *hba, void __iomem *mmio_base, unsigned int irq)
 	async_schedule(ufshcd_async_scan, hba);
 
 	device_enable_async_suspend(dev);
-	ufshcd_pm_qos_init(hba);
+	/*
+	 * The request is 0 whenever the host clocks are on. A host that
+	 * neither scales nor gates its clocks, nor runtime suspends, keeps
+	 * them on from here to system suspend, so the request would hold
+	 * every CPU in its shallowest idle state all that time. Leave it off
+	 * there; pm_qos_enable can still turn it on.
+	 */
+	if (ufshcd_is_clkscaling_supported(hba) || ufshcd_is_clkgating_allowed(hba) ||
+	    ufshcd_is_rpm_autosuspend_allowed(hba))
+		ufshcd_pm_qos_init(hba);
 	return 0;
 
 out_release:
